WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/ai/AIDataRepairSuggestions.tsx — the Helix data-repair-suggestions card. It is
  `withAiFeature('data-repair-suggestions', InnerSection)` (a `useAiEnabled` gate; disabled ⇒ the HOC
  renders `null`). InnerSection uses `useTranslation` + `useAiStream({ url: '/ai/system/data-repair/
  draft', body: {}, onEvent: noop })` and renders the shared `AIFeatureCard` with title
  `t('dataRepair.aiSuggestions.title','Helix repair suggestions')`, a propose-only description
  (`dataRepair.aiSuggestions.description`), button `t('dataRepair.aiSuggestions.button','Draft repair
  plan')`, badge `t('dataRepair.aiSuggestions.badge','Helix')`, `canStart = stream.state !== 'streaming'`
  (the double-submit guard), and the stream handle.

  Critical web contract notes (reproduced, not "fixed"):
    • The body is `useMemo(() => ({}), [])` — EMPTY. There is no vehicle_id / window param; the backend
      reads the in-scope stale-session inventory itself (the canonical ChargingRepo.GetStale /
      DriveRepo.GetStale paths). The native request mirrors this exactly: encodedBody() == "{}".
    • `canStart = stream.state !== 'streaming'` (NOT a vehicle gate, unlike sibling 0005 anomaly). The
      control is live in idle / done / error; disabled only while streaming. stream.start() is a no-op
      while streaming (the hook coalesces; the button mirrors the state machine).
    • Propose-only (I8): the LLM never writes; the typed plan it proposes is rendered, and the user
      applies it via the canonical Save / Close / Discard button on the baseline form below.

  Composed shared primitives reproduced for parity (their native atoms are owned by the P4 component-
  library bundle — out of scope here and not yet present — so they are reproduced as private subviews
  scoped to this surface, the only files this prompt may touch):
    • AIFeatureCard  : GlassPanel → (title + AIBadge) → description → universal "Ask Helix" button
                       (idle "Ask Helix" / streaming "Helix is thinking…"; disabled = !canStart ||
                       isStreaming; aria-label "Ask Helix · {buttonLabel}") → AiOutputPanel.
    • AiOutputPanel  : nothing while idle+empty; "Helix error: {message}" in error; AIThinkingIndicator
                       (shimmer lines + dots) while streaming before the first delta; else the prose.
    • useAiStream    : idle → streaming → (done | error); `delta.text` frames accumulate; a non-OK HTTP
                       response finalises as "stream_http_{status}"; unknown SSE event types dropped.

